        "id": "d00d0001",
        "type": "tab",
        "label": "S2 - Boiler (OMBC) demo - v2 DESIGN MOCK",
        "disabled": false,
        "info": "DESIGN MOCK for openspec/changes/add-control-type-nodes - NOT a working example.\n\n's2-ombc' and 's2-ombc-config' are not implemented yet. If imported, Node-RED will show them as unrecognized-type placeholder boxes. This file exists purely to visualize the wiring shape proposed in design.md, using the shipped examples/boiler-ombc-demo.json as the 'before' baseline for comparison.\n\nWhat changed vs. the current example:\n- s2-rm drops to 3 outputs (no more 'schedule' port).\n- controlTypeConfig moves off s2-rm onto a new s2-ombc-config node.\n- s2-ombc resolves the instruction into msg.topic + msg.ombc directly - the old 'switch on instruction's operation mode' + two 'remember: <mode>' Change nodes (3 nodes, only there to record which mode is active) collapse into a single Change node.\n- Sending OMBC.Status back to the CEM is no longer automatic (session.ts used to fire it at instruction-accept time). It's now an explicit step: once the simulated relay confirms it switched, that confirmation is echoed back into s2-ombc, which emits an UpdateStatus command wired straight into s2-rm's input.",
        "env": []
    },
